ards.\n- **Raise 100**: Small probe bet for value/protection; keeps bluff-catchers in.\n- **Larger raise (e.g., 500+)**: Builds pot but might scare off worse hands; less effective here due to low coordination.\n\nReason:  \nTop pair, top kicker is likely best hand now. Opponent’s check suggests hesitation. A small continuation-style bet (even as little as 100) serves both value and protection purposes. It discourages draws and extracts chips from weaker holdings like middle pair or ace high. With 19.5K behind, a 100-chip bet is minimally risky and maximizes expected value against a wide range.\n\nAnswer: 100'}
